<VI _name="lvdqmh_new_unit_test.vi" description="Headless DQMH New Unit Test. Creates the unit test for ONE request event of ONE DQMH module in the ACTIVE project by calling Delacor's own scripting VIs as STATIC subVIs - the same chain Delacor's Testing Tools\5CNew DQMH Unit Test.vi runs behind its dialog.\0A\0AChain\3A Parse Project for DQMH Modules.vi -> pick the module by NAME -> Get All Events in Module.vi (Request events only\2C Delacor's own setting for unit tests) -> pick the event by NAME -> Script Unit Test.vi -> Close Scripting References.vi on every parsed module.\0A\0AWHY ONE HIERARCHY. Module Info carries thirteen refnums that LabVIEW releases when the VI that opened them stops. Running the parse as its own top-level VI therefore hands the scripter dead references. Here the parse and the scripter are subVIs of this one VI\2C so the references stay alive - the shape Delacor uses in Validate DQMH Module (Headless).vi. The other modules are closed in parallel with the scripting\2C as Delacor's own menu VI does.\0A\0ANOT FOUND IS NOT AN ERROR HERE. Module Index -1\2C Event Index -1 or Any Dirty Modules? TRUE mean nothing was scripted\3B the caller turns that into its own error. Module Names and Event Names list what was found\2C so a caller can report the real spellings. Event Names stays empty when the module was not selected.\0A\0ARequires DQMH installed\2C a project OPEN AND ACTIVE in the IDE\2C and no unsaved module. Generated by LabVIEWMCP\3B the Delacor VIs it calls belong to the user's DQMH installation and are not shipped with it.">
